on was not present at the feature commit","effective_substrate_porosity now uses surface-layer porosity (first non-zero-depth layer) instead of depth-weighted average — addresses the heterogeneous-stack diffusion bottleneck","estimate_substrate_o2_demand_rate now includes substrate microfauna respiration via estimate_substrate_microfauna_o2_demand_mg_per_s","SubstrateSurface habitat = footprint + oxic interstitial area; SubstrateDeep habitat = suboxic interstitial area — verified in compute_substrate_surface and compute_substrate_deep in habitat.rs","Per-zone accessors for volume, pore volume, colonizable area, and nutrient availability are all implemented on TankState"],"findings_or_gaps":["REGRESSION: `molt_stress_warning_has_cause_codes` test fails at HEAD (b107cf8). The plan_and_implement c2r2 checkpoint introduced a large shrimp molt refactor (per-stage timers, new mineral modifier function, MoltFailure event kind, new ShrimpRuntimeParams fields) that is out of scope for the substrate oxic/suboxic zone bead and breaks an existing test. The feature commit 929daa5 is clean.","SCOPE CREEP: The b107cf8 checkpoint adds ~200 lines of shrimp molt system changes (per-stage molt timers in StageCohort, molt_mineral_modifier with Ca/Mg individual scoring, MoltFailure event, 5 new ShrimpRuntimeParams fields) that belong to a separate bead. These changes alter simulation dynamics enough to break the events test and potentially the reproduction baseline scenario.","MINOR: The dirty worktree contains additional uncommitted changes to shrimp.rs and tank_scenarios that attempt to fix the regression but do not succeed (the events test still fails even with those changes applied)."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Revert the shrimp molt refactor from b107cf8 back to the 929daa5 state. The substrate microfauna demand and surface-layer porosity changes (the two accepted final-review amendments) should be applied cleanly on top of 929daa5 WITHOUT the shrimp/biology/events/snapshot changes that were bundled into the same checkpoint.","Once the shrimp molt refactor is cleanly separated, verify that `cargo test -p tank_core` passes in full (including `molt_stress_warning_has_cause_codes`) and `cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_baseline_scenarios` passes (including `controlled_ideal_reproduction_path_still_hatches`)."],"outcome":"request_changes"},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6b7d470c-37a9-42fd-9438-d977d974cdae"}
